    {
      "title": "‘Leon Black is hiding behind litigation’: outrage after billionaire sues Congress over subpoenas for Epstein investigation – live",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/sep/03/donald-trump-immigration-tariffs-canada-trade-iran-jd-vance-latest-news-updates",
      "description": "<p>Republican oversight chair James Comer says he will speak to committee about next steps as Democrat calls for holding billionaire in contempt for defying two subpoenas</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/news/2026/feb/17/sign-up-for-the-breaking-news-us-email-to-get-newsletter-alerts-direct-to-your-inbox?utm_medium=ACQUISITIONS_STANDFIRST&amp;utm_campaign=BN22326&amp;utm_content=signup&amp;utm_term=standfirst&amp;utm_source=GUARDIAN_WEB\">Sign up for US Breaking News emails</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>Republican oversight chair James Comer has also weighed in on Leon Black not sitting for a deposition about his ties to Jeffrey Epstein.</strong> The billionaire financier, who has denied wrongdoing, filed suit against the oversight committee Thursday alleging the subpoenas were improper.</p><p>“It’s a shame Leon Black is hiding behind litigation rather than provide answers to the American people. Our investigation is examining how the federal government for decades failed survivors of Jeffery Epstein and Ghislaine Maxwell’s crimes and how Mr. Epstein sought to curry favor with influential individuals to avoid scrutiny,” Comer said in a statement. “Mr. Black’s testimony is crucial to our investigation as he was one of Mr. Epstein’s fee paying clients and has several nondisclosure agreements.”</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/sep/03/donald-trump-immigration-tariffs-canada-trade-iran-jd-vance-latest-news-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-03T15:03:53"
    },
    {
      "title": "Leon Black fails to appear for US House deposition about Epstein ties",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/03/jeffrey-epstein-leon-black-congress-deposition",
      "description": "<p>Billionaire financier, who previously walked out of a deposition, instead launches lawsuit against the committee</p><p>Billionaire financier Leon Black did not appear Thursday in front of the House oversight committee for a scheduled deposition about his ties to <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/jeffrey-epstein\">Jeffrey Epstein</a>, and has instead launched a lawsuit against the committee arguing that it does not have the authority to compel him to turn over non-disclosure agreements.</p><p>Black was a top Epstein client over several years, and the committee is investigating the men’s relationship as well as the existence of any NDAs that Epstein may have helped Black craft. Black, whose name has <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/feb/02/epstein-files-new-batch\">come up</a> repeatedly in the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/feb/10/jeffrey-epstein-brad-karp-woman-deported\">Epstein files</a>, has denied wrongdoing. Black also said that he regrets dealing with Epstein.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/03/jeffrey-epstein-leon-black-congress-deposition\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-03T14:08:26"
    },
